      "message": "fix(xtask): --failed reruns the steps that a failed build stopped\n\nEach step that a failed build stops gets a log with the one line\n`not run (build failed: <step>)`, and `select::log_failed` reads it as a\nfailed step. So `--failed gate-logs/<run>` runs the build step and each\nstopped step, not the build step alone. The BUILD FAULT block shows only\nfor a `--no-run` step: a test whose output quotes E0786 gets none.\n\nReview of PR #3708.\n\nRefs #3601\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
